<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mexica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mexica were the Nahuatl-speaking people who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a> and led the Aztec Triple Alliance. They rose from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> service to dominance after defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanecs</a> in the fifteenth century. Their warrior culture and tribute system were central to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p></div>
